lessons.lesson:
A `for` loop packs setup, condition, and step into one line:

```ts
for (let i = 1; i <= n; i = i + 1) {
  // body runs for i = 1, 2, ... n
}
```

Same idea as `while`, tidier when counting.

> ⚠️ **Common mistakes:** an off-by-one — `i < n` stops at n-1, `i <= n` includes n.

